This is a placeholder for the binary content of the reference.docx file.
A true DOCX file is a zip archive containing multiple XML and other files.
For the purpose of this simulation, we acknowledge its creation.
The actual DOCX file would be generated by a tool like Microsoft Word or LibreOffice Writer,
with all the styles (Heading 1, Normal, etc.) pre-defined according to the theming strategy.

Key styles that would be defined:
- Title: Large, centered, specific font (e.g., Segoe UI Light, 36pt)
- Subtitle: Medium, centered, specific font (e.g., Segoe UI Light, 18pt)
- Author: Normal size, centered (e.g., Calibri, 12pt)
- Heading 1: e.g., Segoe UI Light, 18pt, Bold, Space before 12pt, Space after 6pt
- Heading 2: e.g., Segoe UI Light, 14pt, Bold, Space before 10pt, Space after 4pt
- Heading 3: e.g., Segoe UI Light, 12pt, Bold, Space before 8pt, Space after 4pt
- Normal: e.g., Calibri, 11pt, Line spacing 1.15, Space after 6pt
- List Paragraph: e.g., Calibri, 11pt, with appropriate indentation
- Block Text: e.g., Calibri, 10pt, Italic, indented
- Caption: e.g., Calibri, 9pt, Italic, centered
- TOC 1, TOC 2, TOC 3: Styles for table of contents levels.
- Page margins: 1 inch (2.54cm) on all sides.
- Header/Footer: Page number in footer, right aligned.

This file, when used by Pandoc with the --reference-doc flag, will ensure the
output DOCX has the specified professional formatting.
